1_data/10_raw/102_fna/1020_timelimit_waiver_docs/**/*.pdf
1_data/10_raw/102_fna/1020_timelimit_waiver_docs/**/*.doc
1_data/10_raw/102_fna/1020_timelimit_waiver_docs/**/*.docx
# FNA application ("State Requests and Data") zips + everything extracted from them.
# Contents ignored, directory kept: 2123_download_fna_application_zips.py stages here.
1_data/10_raw/102_fna/1023_application_docs/**
!1_data/10_raw/102_fna/1023_application_docs/.gitkeep
# FNA extraction outputs -- IGNORED, including the model JSONs.
#
# This reverses an earlier intent (never actually executed: no extraction JSON was
# ever committed). The old comment argued the JSONs must be versioned because
# agentic extraction is NOT deterministic -- the NC run-1 vs run-2 replication
# (2026-08-10) showed independent runs of the same prompt/schema/model differing on
# transcription (Pasguotank -> Pasquotank) and on judgment calls (FY2013 criterion
# null vs eb_trigger) -- so a prompt revision can only be scored against a FIXED
# baseline. That premise still holds. Versioning is the wrong way to hold it:
#
#   1. It contradicts the blinding rule (75f4a89). Extraction subagents have full
#      repo access and must not read any other arm's output. A tracked JSON is
#      reachable through `git show`/`git log -p` even after 8a2dbe5 wiped the
#      working tree, so tracking re-opens the exact channel blinding closes.
#   2. The baseline that has to be fixed is the (spec, model) pair, and that is
#      already pinned by run_id = sha256(instruction + prompt + schema + model_tag),
#      which IS versioned -- the spec files are. The ledger records which run_id
#      produced which document. An arm is identified by its run_id, not by a blob.
#   3. Arms are large and grow with the corpus (v1_5 is 20MB / 649 documents at 34
#      states, with 16 states still to extract).
#
# The consequence, stated plainly: an arm's JSONs live ONLY in the working tree. A
# deleted arm is gone -- re-running the same spec does not reproduce it. Treat an
# arm directory as a lab notebook, not as a build artifact.
1_data/10_raw/102_fna/1022_extractions/**/*.json
1_data/10_raw/102_fna/1022_extractions/*.csv

# GEO REFERENCE (state geography context build)
# Raw Census/BLS reference pulls + the pinned us-atlas topology: regenerable via
# `make geo_fetch` and `make viz_fetch`. Contents ignored, directory kept.
1_data/10_raw/103_geo/**
!1_data/10_raw/103_geo/.gitkeep
# Hand-curated county-change log: versioned source input (overrides blanket *.csv).
!0_lit/01_geo/010_county_changes_1997_present.csv

# PROGRESS TABLE (2226)
# Hand-curated tier + geo-wart registry: versioned source input, NOT regenerable --
# the tier assignments and the prose warts are judgments, not derived counts.
# (Overrides the blanket *.csv ignore, same as the county-change log above.)
!2_scripts/22_extract/222_fna_waivers/2226a_state_tier_registry.csv

# PRESENTATION (built outputs)
# 6_present holds BUILT pages, not sources -- the sources are 2_scripts/26_present.
# The waiver map is 26MB per rebuild (14MB payload + a 12MB self-contained page) and
# is fully reproducible with `make viz` from an extraction arm + the pinned topology,
# so it is ignored; the shareable copy is the published Claude Artifact. Every builder
# mkdirs its own output tree, so a clean checkout rebuilds without the directory
# existing -- the .gitkeep is there to show a reader where the output lands.
6_present/61_waiver_map/*.json
6_present/61_waiver_map/*.html
!6_present/61_waiver_map/.gitkeep
# LaTeX build turds (beamer slides). The .tex + figs/ are the source and track;
# the compiled .pdf tracks too, as 5_write's PDFs already do.
*.aux
*.log
*.nav
*.out
*.snm
*.toc
*.synctex.gz

# SCRIPTS
# Helper scripts and cache
2_scripts/22_extract/221_abawd_waivers/__pycache__/
2_scripts/22_extract/222_fna_waivers/__pycache__/

# WORKLOG (session research record) -- track the CSV database
# (overriding any global *.csv ignore). Entries are .md and track
# by default; session-id state lives globally, not in the repo.
!.worklog/worklog.csv
